{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Your data — bindsight{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Your data</h1>
<p class="lede">
  A counts matrix and a sample design table naming a two-level factor. Nothing
  on this path knows about cancer — <code>tumor</code> and <code>normal</code>
  are values you supply, not values the code expects.
</p>

<div class="card">
  <h2 class="card__title">Files</h2>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="counts">Counts matrix <span class="muted">(.tsv, .txt, .gz)</span></label>
    <input type="file" id="counts" accept=".tsv,.txt,.gz">
    <p class="field__help">Genes as rows, samples as columns, integer counts.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="design">Sample design table <span class="muted">(.tsv, .txt, .gz)</span></label>
    <input type="file" id="design" accept=".tsv,.txt,.gz">
    <p class="field__help">One row per sample, with a column naming the condition.</p>
  </div>

  <div id="checks" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="false"></div>
</div>

<div class="note note--info">
  <span class="note__glyph" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
  <div class="note__body">
    <p class="small" style="margin:0">
      Files are checked the moment you choose them — shape, separator, and
      whether the sample names in the two tables agree. The contrast levels are
      read from your design file and offered back to you, rather than typed: a
      mistyped level used to surface as a generic pipeline failure minutes
      later, after the cohort had already been processed.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
{#- The checker is bindsight/report/web/static/your_data_check.js, shared with
    the published documentation site so the two cannot diverge. -#}
<script src="/static/your_data_check.js"></script>
{% endblock %}
